g valuable assets [Data: Entities (61); Relationships (138, 164)]. The blood-pact between M. Gustave and Zero involves selling the \\\"Boy with Apple\\\" painting, leaving the country, and sharing the proceeds, underscoring the painting's economic significance [Data: Relationships (339)].\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Legal Entanglements and M. Gustave's Pursuit of Justice\",\n      \"explanation\": \"M. Gustave is accused of Madame D's murder, a charge he vehemently denies, leading to his pursuit as a \\\"fugitive from justice\\\" by Henckels [Data: Entities (48, 385); Relationships (814)]. He is arrested and jailed, where he diligently works with fellow convicts to plan and execute an elaborate escape from a prison-castle [Data: Entities (48, 386, 410, 413); Relationships (815)]. During his ordeal, he gives testimony to a jury and judge [Data: Entities (420, 421); Relationships (930, 931)]. He is eventually cleared of the murder charges, having an alibi involving the Duke of Westfalia's wife [Data: Entities (48)]. Despite his exoneration, his journey concludes tragically when he is arrested and later shot by soldiers in black uniforms [Data: Entities (48)].\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Serge's Betrayal, Witness Role, and Tragic Demise\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Serge served in a butler-like capacity, assisting M. Gustave and Zero, but M. Gustave held a negative view of him due to a past betrayal [Data: Entities (162)]. Serge was an official witness to Madame D's second will, which was contingent on her death by murder [Data: Entities (162, 368); Relationships (793)]. He became a key witness in M. Gustave's murder case, having ostensibly seen the alleged events, and revealed critical information to M. Gustave before his death [Data: Entities (162)]. Serge's personal life was marked by tragedy, as his family was murdered, and he is implied to be the brother of a sister whose severed head was found [Data: Entities (162, 369); Relationships (772)]